Hair (served by the app; not MIT)
================================================================================
The strand files (*.strands.bin, about 220 MB) are not in this repository; the
app serves them from Vercel Blob (web/scripts/upload-hair.ts). Their thumbnails
and web/public/models/hair/index.json are in the repository. Each style's author
and pack are listed in index.json.

web/public/models/hair/haircs/ (223 styles): derived from HairCS, "HairCS:
Reconstructing Strand-Based Hair from Hair Cards", Lu, Wang, Shen, Zheng, Jiang,
Yin Yang, Kui Wu, 2026, https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.16465; dataset
https://huggingface.co/datasets/HairCS2027/HairCS. Licensed CC BY-NC 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/): NON-COMMERCIAL USE ONLY. Changes:
refitted onto the GNM head, cleaned of stray strands, resampled and re-encoded
(pipeline/src/ftv_pipeline/haircs_review.py, import_hair.py). See
web/public/models/hair/haircs/LICENSE.md.

web/public/models/hair/bystedt-* (4 styles): from "Hair Styles"
(hair_nodes-female_hair_styles.blend, https://www.blender.org/download/demo-files/)
by Daniel Bystedt, licensed CC BY-SA 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). Changes: the evaluated strands
were refitted onto the GNM head, resampled and re-encoded
(pipeline/src/ftv_pipeline/import_hair.py). These derived files are shared under
CC BY-SA 4.0.

web/public/models/hair/side_part.*: a procedural groom grown by this project
(pipeline/src/ftv_pipeline/groom.py, config/grooms.toml), MIT.

================================================================================
Add-ons (generated by this project, MIT)
================================================================================
Everything in web/public/models/addons/ is generated by this project's pipeline
and released under the MIT License: strand eyebrows (brow_strands.py), strand
eyelashes (lash_strands.py), stubble masks, shell beards and strand beards
(stubble.py, beard_strands.py) and glasses (glasses_gen.py, glasses_fit.py).

The eyebrows and beards are grown inside outlines read from shape guides saved in
pipeline/config/guides/, which are data derived from MakeHuman assets released
under CC0 1.0 Universal (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/); no
attribution is required, and we give it anyway:
- brows/ (eleven cards): MakeHuman system eyebrows, Data Collection AB, Joel
  Palmius, Jonas Hauquier (2020);
- landmarks.json (eleven points used by the glasses fit): the MakeHuman hm08 base
  mesh, same authors and release;
- beards/: four beards from the MakeHuman community "bodyparts05" pack
  (https://static.makehumancommunity.org/assets/assetpacks/bodyparts05.html):
  Rehman Polanski (viking-beard, moustache), WDG (scruffy-beard) (*),
  grinsegold (full-beard) (*).
  (*) The pack page lists these as CC0; the header of their .mhclo source files
  says "license AGPL3". This project relies on the pack page.

